  "interpretation": [
    "The no-framework controls demonstrate that fixed full-GC checkpoints can leave targets observable without a Bun Native or framework implementation.",
    "The positive no-framework result is development-only in these matrices. It does not reproduce or explain the original native AOT mid-run failure.",
    "All sleep(0), sleep(1), and setTimeout(0) promises were pending at synchronous inspection. Promise.resolve was fulfilled. All targets were already collected by the initial Bun.gc(true) in that control.",
    "Changing full-GC entry point preserved the development-only positives in v3. It did not identify or remove the retaining root.",
    "Missing incoming graph edges are not proof of a conservative root: the snapshot omits some edges and itself performs another collection.",
    "Renderer WeakRef and benchmark oracles remain unchanged. Deterministic ownership, mutation counts and callback revocation remain mandatory. No accepted matched timing comparison is derived from failed/incomplete trials."
  ],
